  "text": "all right we're recording okay i'm here with max from mountainside er so max why don't you tell us what you do here and how long you've been working here for sure so i'm a driver here at mountainside er i've been here going on three months i'm mainly a driver but i operate the loader that you can see behind us when needed and i basically just haul material to sites and from quarries and uh it's pretty much it for now what's your favorite part about the job my favorite part i like operating heavy equipment so operating that loader is my favorite part yeah were you the kid who loved the tractors when you were growing up and this is like it's like playing with like yeah big boy toys exactly yeah that's awesome yeah what is your least favorite part of the job at least favorite part um just the super long hours in the truck yeah yeah what's the biggest thing you've learned since you've been here biggest thing that i learned would be um operating equipment because before this position i did not ever operate any equipment so operating that loader would be the biggest thing so far i'm looking forward to operating the skid steer that john has as well and any other future equipment that he gets yeah okay what about biggest life lesson learned from operating heavy equipment and working at mountainside er that's your takeaway that let's say you let's say you don't do this some point in the future what life lesson will you take with you in the future patience this this job teaches you a lot of patience and when i started driving i didn't have much patience and i quickly learned that yeah with all the people on the road you know all the stunts that they pull and just the amount of responsibility that you have with all this weight you know uh it's no joke and responsibility and patience for sure yeah yeah that's great awesome thank you max you're no joke and patience for sure yeah you're welcome",
